###
Addon syntax, all in one file.

Nothing here is core Skript. Every line belongs to an addon, and what you see
depends on what your server actually has installed:

  * addon installed  — hover, completion and colour, exactly like core syntax
  * addon missing    — the line stays plain and says nothing

That silence is deliberate. There are 168 published addons and 12,877 patterns
between them; guessing would mean a wall of false errors on every real server.
So the extension tells you what it *found*, never what it assumed.

To see the difference, point the server at a real server directory — it reads
the JARs in `plugins/` and loads syntax only for what is genuinely there:

  "lsp": { "skript-lsp": { "initialization_options": {
    "serverPath": "/srv/minecraft/my-server"
  } } }

Every line below is checked against the published catalog by
`crates/skript-docs/tests/addon_examples.rs`, which asserts that each one
resolves to the addon whose heading it sits under. Addon syntax written from
memory is wrong surprisingly often, and a wrong line here would be invisible:
it would look exactly like an addon you have not installed.
###

# === SkBee ===
#
# The most widely installed addon by some distance — NBT, item components,
# recipes, world border and chunk generation.

on virtual furnace smelt:
	stop

on virtual furnace fuel burning:
	stop

on quit:
	apply tool component to player's tool

# === skript-reflect ===
#
# Java interop and custom events. Mixed into most large projects, and the reason
# `import:` shows up at the top of so many scripts.

on custom event "my-plugin-event":
	stop

on join:
	call event {_event}
	delay the current effect

# === SkQuery ===
#
# One of the oldest addons still in use. Mostly extra events.

on sheep dye:
	stop

on vehicle collide with block:
	stop

# === TuSKe ===
#
# GUIs and clans. Long unmaintained, still everywhere.

on clan chat:
	stop

on clan create:
	stop

on ally clan add:
	stop

# === skRayFall ===
#
# Citizens NPC control, holograms and JSON messages.

on join:
	make citizen 1 hold a diamond sword
	make citizen 2 look at player's location
	make citizen 3 invulnerable
	give npc 4 the look close trait

# === MundoSK ===
#
# Custom world generators, packets and tab completion.

on tab complete:
	stop

on quit:
	load chunk {_chunk}

# === Lusk ===
#
# A newer, actively maintained addon — anvil GUIs, entity behaviour and a large
# expression library.

on join:
	randomly teleport player
	teleport player towards target entity
	close lusk anvil gui {_gui}
